+// youtubeStatCountExpr is the SQL for one YouTube statistics count (viewCount,
+// likeCount) as a BIGINT. YouTube can store an empty string for a hidden count, and
+// Postgres rejects a bare ::BIGINT cast on it, failing the whole list query. Anything
+// that is not plain digits is therefore NULL (unknown) instead. Every sort and filter
+// on these counts goes through here so the guard lives in one place. field is a fixed
+// statistics key, never request input.
